From 0a21e9f9ada64fb9af39a186d8cee15f315a3631 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jellyfrog <Jellyfrog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:23:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libsnmp: Add a cache of parsed MIB files

Rebuilding the MIB tree for another list of modules (shutdown_mib(),
init_mib()) parses every module file again, including the ones that
every list shares. With netsnmp_mib_cache_enable(1), what parsing a file
did is recorded, and reading the file again replays it instead of
parsing: module starts, IMPORTS (read again, through the cache), modules
read for MODULE and SUPPORTS clauses, textual conventions, and the
nodes, which are linked into the tree as after parsing.

Entries are keyed by file path, mtime and size, MIB directories and
parser options. Files that fail to parse, and files whose parse looks up
a textual convention imported from a module that is not found, are not
cached.

parse_imports() is split into tokenizing and process_imports() so that
replaying an IMPORTS clause runs the same code.
---
 include/net-snmp/library/parse.h |   4 +
 snmplib/parse.c                  | 818 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 773 insertions(+), 49 deletions(-)

